CONCL=[
("The Major Funds levy has been $755.3M since FY2022, when the County cut it $70M (8.5%) from $825.3M. FY2027 is the 5th straight budget with no increase.",LIME),
("From FY2017 to FY2027 the Major Funds budget grew 28.7% ($2.97B to $3.82B) while the levy fell 7.6% ($817.0M to $755.3M). The levy's share of the budget dropped from 27.5% to 19.7%.",LIME),
("Sales tax filled most of the space: budgeted sales tax rose 50% ($1,142.5M to $1,713.2M) and is now 45.3% of Major Funds revenue. NIFA says 2026 growth is only 0.39% after inflation.",TEAL),
("Reserves fill the rest: $43.5M budgeted in FY2027 and $476.5M appropriated across the plan, out of $615.9M on hand. Reserves are down $135.0M since 12/31/2024.",TEAL),
("Tax-cap math (derived): 2% of the levy is $15.1M a year. Taking 2% each year from FY2023 would put the FY2027 levy at about $833.9M, $78.6M a year more, or about $232.7M left on the table over five years.",BLUE2),
("Even a full 2% increase would replace only about a third of the $43.5M reserve draw. Replacing it alone needs a 5.8% levy increase (derived).",BLUE2),
("Closing NIFA's FY2027 gap without reserves needs $104.0M–$189.0M, a 13.8%–25.0% levy increase. By FY2030 it is $142.5M–$295.1M, or 18.9%–39.1%. Anything above the cap needs an override (derived).",PINK),
("FY2025 showed the strain: a ($56.0M) control-period deficit, ($129.4M) restated, equal to 17.1% of a year's levy. NIFA projects deficits above the 1% trigger through FY2030, so the control period stays.",PINK),
("Tax certiorari is the hidden levy cost: $292.7M owed at 12/31/2025 (38.8% of a year's levy), versus the County's own $160.0M target. Only $15.0M a year is budgeted in the out-years.",PINK),
("NIFA ties the refund burden to the assessment freeze, which it says shifts taxes onto owners who do not grieve. The County has refused NIFA's assessment audit since April 2026.",PINK),
("NIFA does not call for a levy increase in the reports reviewed. It calls the plan structurally imbalanced and says reserve reliance with no contingency is \"a sign of fiscal weakness.\" The County says the plan is structurally balanced.",LIME),
("Labor will push harder: police/corrections contracts were extended one year at 4.5%, with only $30.0M a year carried for later rounds. NIFA votes on those MOUs and the FY2027 plan on Nov 19.",LIME),
]
LEVY=[("One year at the 2% cap","755.3 × 2%","$15.1M"),("FY2027 levy if +2%/yr since FY2023","755.3 × 1.02^5","$833.9M (+$78.6M/yr)"),("Levy forgone FY2023–FY2027 at 2%/yr","Σ 755.3 × (1.02^k − 1), k=1..5","$232.7M"),("Replace FY2027 budgeted reserves","43.5 ÷ 755.3","+5.8%"),("FY2027 gap w/o reserves, low–high","(60.5 or 145.5) + 43.5 ÷ 755.3","+13.8% to +25.0%"),("FY2030 gap w/o reserves, low–high","(116.0 or 268.6) + 26.5 ÷ 755.3","+18.9% to +39.1%"),("FY2025 restated deficit vs levy","129.4 ÷ 755.3","17.1%"),("Tax-cert liability vs levy","292.7 ÷ 755.3","38.8%")]
